# Credentials Setup Guide

> All steps sourced from official documentation as of March 2026.

---

## Your [.env](file:///c:/Suraj/SPPU/Project/AUTOMATIC/.env) File — What You Need

| Variable | Where to Get | Required For |
|---|---|---|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Google AI Studio | All AI features |
| `META_APP_ID` | Meta App Dashboard | Instagram publishing |
| `META_APP_SECRET` | Meta App Dashboard | Instagram publishing |
| `JWT_SECRET` | Generate yourself | User authentication |
| `ENCRYPTION_KEY` | Generate yourself | Token encryption |

---

## 1. Gemini API Key (5 minutes)

> [!TIP]
> This is the easiest credential — just one click.

1. Go to **[Google AI Studio — API Keys](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)**
2. Sign in with your Google account
3. Click **"Create API Key"**
4. Select a Google Cloud project (or let it create a default one)
5. Copy the key

```env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
```

**Free tier limits** (no credit card needed):
- Gemini 2.5 Flash: 1500 requests/day
- Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite: 4000 requests/day
- Gemini Embeddings: 1500 requests/day
- Image generation: Included

> **Docs**: [ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/api-key](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/api-key)

---

## 2. Meta App for Instagram (30-60 minutes)

### Prerequisites
- A **Facebook account**
- An **Instagram Business or Creator (Professional) account**
- A [**Meta Business Portfolio**](https://business.facebook.com/) (free to create)

### Step-by-Step

#### Step 1: Create Meta App
1. Go to **[developers.facebook.com/apps](https://developers.facebook.com/apps)**
2. Click **"Create App"**
3. Connect a business (you can do this later too)
4. Select use case: **"Other"**
5. Select app type: **"Business"**
6. Add app name (e.g. "InstaAutomate") + your contact email
7. Click **Next** — you'll land on the app dashboard

#### Step 2: Add Instagram Product
1. In the app dashboard, scroll to find **"Instagram"**
2. Click **"Set up"**
3. Select **"API setup with Instagram login"** (this is what our system uses)

#### Step 3: Add Your Instagram Account
1. Go to **Instagram > API Setup with Instagram login** in the left menu
2. In section **"1. Generate access tokens"**, click **"Add"**
3. Log in with your Instagram account (must be **public**)
4. This gives you access tokens for testing

#### Step 4: Get Your App ID & Secret

> [!IMPORTANT]
> These are the values you put in your [.env](file:///c:/Suraj/SPPU/Project/AUTOMATIC/.env) file.

1. In the left menu, go to **Instagram > API setup with Instagram login**
2. Look at section **"3. Set up Instagram business login"**
3. Click **"Business login settings"**
4. You'll see:
   - **Instagram App ID** → This is your `META_APP_ID`
   - **Instagram App Secret** → This is your `META_APP_SECRET`

```env
META_APP_ID=990602627938098
META_APP_SECRET=your-secret-here
```

#### Step 5: Configure Business Login
1. In **Business login settings**, add:
   - **Redirect URI**: `http://localhost:8000/api/instagram/callback` (for development)
   - **Deauthorize callback URL**: `http://localhost:8000/api/instagram/deauthorize` (optional)
   - **Data deletion request URL**: `http://localhost:8000/api/instagram/data-deletion` (optional)
2. Click **Save**

#### Step 6: App Review (Required for Publishing)

> [!CAUTION]
> You **cannot publish content** to Instagram until App Review is completed and you get **Advanced Access** for the `instagram_business_content_publish` permission.

1. Go to **App Review > Requests** in the left menu
2. You need these permissions approved:
   - `instagram_business_basic` (Required)
   - `instagram_business_content_publish` (Required)
   - `instagram_business_manage_insights` (Recommended — for analytics)
3. For each permission, you'll need to:
   - Explain your use case
   - Upload **screen recordings** showing how your app uses each permission
   - Confirm your app can be tested externally

> **Note**: If your app is just for **your own accounts** (Standard Access), you can test with accounts you've added to the App Dashboard **before** completing full App Review.

> **Docs**: [Create a Meta App](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/instagram-platform/instagram-api-with-instagram-login/create-a-meta-app-with-instagram)

---

## 3. Self-Generated Credentials

### JWT Secret
```bash
python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
```
```env
JWT_SECRET=paste-the-output-here
```

### Encryption Key (Fernet)
```bash
python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
```
```env
ENCRYPTION_KEY=paste-the-output-here
```

---

## 4. Complete [.env](file:///c:/Suraj/SPPU/Project/AUTOMATIC/.env) Example

```env
# ========== GEMINI AI ==========
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-key

# ========== META / INSTAGRAM ==========
META_APP_ID=your-instagram-app-id
META_APP_SECRET=your-instagram-app-secret

# ========== DATABASE ==========
DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./data/automation.db

# ========== AUTHENTICATION ==========
JWT_SECRET=your-generated-jwt-secret
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your-generated-fernet-key

# ========== APPLICATION ==========
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
DEBUG=false
```

---

## What You Can Do Without Meta Credentials

Even **before** setting up the Meta App, all of these work with just the Gemini API key:
- Content generation (text + images)
- Trend research via Google Search grounding
- Brand voice analysis
- Content calendar generation
- Analytics quality checks
- The entire AI brain/memory system

**Instagram publishing** is the only feature that requires the Meta credentials.

